# openHC feature: zigbee (kernel half) — USB-serial transport for a USB-bridged
# NCP. The EA family reaches its EM357 through a Silabs CP2104 (10c4:ea60); these
# three symbols are what turn that bridge into /dev/ttyUSB0.
#
# Harmless on boards whose NCP is on a NATIVE UART (ca1 ttymxc4, hc800 ttyS4):
# there is no CP2104, so cp210x simply binds nothing. The USB HOST CONTROLLER
# itself is board hardware, not part of this shared feature — it stays in each
# board's own fragment (on the EA that is the EHCI block in ea/common, which also
# needs patch 0014 to bring the TransDimension core out of -110 at all).
CONFIG_USB=y
CONFIG_USB_SERIAL=y
CONFIG_USB_SERIAL_CP210X=y
